WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:13.880
<v Speaker 1>Hey, we're back. This is Justin Gary. I'm here with Scott Larabee, the DCI Program Manager, and we are standing in front of a giant tower of money. Scott, could you explain to us what this giant tower of money is?</v>

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:32.520
<v Speaker 2>I can. This is a visual representation of all the money we've given away since 1996 when the Pro Tour started. So you can see down the side here. It's kind of like a thermometer. 96 we gave away 1,000,043 and then in 97 we gave them. It's a progressive total of what we've given away. When you get up to the top,</v>

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:37.990
<v Speaker 2>by the end of the year will have given away about over $21 million, almost 22 million.</v>

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.770
<v Speaker 1>$22 million and and how exactly did you find out all of this information?</v>

00:00:43.780 --> 00:01:02.690
<v Speaker 2>Well, I, I've spent the last four weeks researching it. So we've got, you know, we've got databases, but we paid the money out of and that said who we paid it to and what they breakdown, Where are we? You know, I consulted old sideboard magazines for stuff. Some of the interesting stories were, you know, figuring, remembering that we ran a A-Team pro challenge at pro Tour at</v>

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:36.570
<v Speaker 2>Santa's back in September of 96 and we ran the Type 1 Pro Tour in Dallas. And like nobody had remembered those and they weren't in any lists of anything. And I was at them and remembered them. So I had to research them by getting some old magazines and finding the dollar amounts. So a couple of the other ones where we ran the the team challenge and the draft challenge for the ESPN shows where we gave away a little bit of money before the Masters series. And those weren't listed anywhere either. So it find those and figure out who we paid and how much. And then you know, the researching the Masters money and all the grand prize and how much we paid and all the national championships and how much we paid and</v>

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:44.370
<v Speaker 2>pro tour qualifier money. And we're still, we're actually still doing some research. This is. We're still working on the final totals, but this is a pretty good representation.</v>

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.690
<v Speaker 1>So I notice that you're giving away more and more and more each year. Do you expect that trend to continue?</v>

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:56.120
<v Speaker 2>For gonna give away, by the end of this year we'll have given away a little over $3,000,000 and next year we'll be at about the same level, about $3,000,000 a year.</v>

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:04.170
<v Speaker 1>Well, that's pretty exciting. I'm just going to kind of stand here and admire this money for awhile, and we'll get more from World Championships later.</v>

